From: JorreFog <JorreFog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:52:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ROCKNIXDS: DATE & TIME, the date and time set by hand

ROCKNIX sets the clock only over Wi-Fi (NTP), so a handheld without Wi-Fi kept a wrong date and time with
no way to change it. SYSTEM SETTINGS > DATE & TIME sets the year, month, day, hour and minute (the system
clock, then the RTC in UTC with hwclock); Wi-Fi's time still replaces them once it connects, and a
message says so when Wi-Fi is connected. The time zone
and the 12-hour switch moved there. The time zone list now splits timeinfo's lines as well as its commas
(every zone but the first started with a newline), and only a zone that exists is linked.
---
 es-app/src/guis/GuiMenu.cpp | 147 +++++++++++++++++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 102 insertions(+), 45 deletions(-)

